From 7879d9bdc8f2121fd6c7b3845d80e1ab38e1cc3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 18:04:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/77] sunxi: h713: add the power gate in front of the
 power-on lines

Stock keeps the projector in standby until the power key is pressed; our
U-Boot switched fan, backlight and USB power on unconditionally. Add
CONFIG_H713_POWER_GATE: before h713_poweron_lines(), read RTC GP5
(0x07090114) -- 0 is a cold start and "GATE" a power-off request from
TF-A, both wait for the power key on PL4 (active low, external pull-up,
50 ms debounce, release starts the boot); "RUN1" is a warm start and
boots straight through. U-Boot stamps RUN1 on every path before powering
up, so reboot, crash and watchdog reset never land in the gate. A key
held for 3 s at power-on bypasses the gate once; the env variable
h713_gate=0 disables it without a rebuild. The status LED follows PB5,
so no LED code is needed. Gate on in hy310_qz713_v3_1 and the new test
defconfig hy310_netboot_gate, off in netboot, host and felmmc.

Measured on the HY310 2026-09-08/09; plan doku/103, report doku/nachtlog/S36.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
